  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 410 AM EDT Fri May 15 2026\n\nHigh pressure over the area continues into the extended periods \nkeeping things mostly dry through the beginning of next week. It \ndoes begin to weaken some by the middle of the week but it still \ndominates the overall pattern. The Bermuda high settles across the \narea through Mon/Tue which will keep any approaching \nfronts/shortwaves to well north of our area. This ridge does put GA \nunder southerly flow which will slowly increase moisture across the \narea. By Sunday, with the increased temps (upper 80s to lower 90s) \nand increased moisture we may see an isolated diurnally driven \nshower or two. The limiting factor will be the ridge keeping things \nfairly capped across the state. Towards the end of the longterm, \nthere is an indication that a front will push into the area bringing \nin rainfall Tue/Wed if the front is able to hold together and the \nridge breaks down. We will continue to monitor this pattern to see \njust how strong this ridge ends up being.",
